Verified for this specific build (submissions/mnist/install/lib/libheaan2.so.0.2.0, x86_64 Linux,
CUDA-enabled) by inspecting its dynamic symbol table and runtime dependencies (`ldd`, `nm -D`,
`strings`) rather than assumed from another build of the same library — different HEaaN2 build
configurations (CPU vs CUDA, target architecture) can embed or link a different dependency set.

No third-party source is statically embedded in this build (checked for the components CryptoLab's
other HEaaN2-based benchmark submissions have listed, e.g. GNU Quadmath and the public-domain
Keccak/tweetfips202 implementation from kyber — neither appears in this binary's symbol table).

